#   crates/pi-natives           arboard + clipboard/desktop modules become
#                               cfg(not(target_os = "android")) — arboard has no
#                               Android backend.
#   crates/pi-shell             compiles its Linux process backend on Android too.
#   crates/pi-builtins          Bionic-compatible process discovery (/proc) and
#                               rsync syscalls.
#   crates/pi-vfs               defines AT_EACCESS locally: the libc crate omits
#                               it for Android.
#   packages/natives/scripts/   scopes RUSTC_BOOTSTRAP to xutf,pi_natives so a
#     build-bindings.ts         stable rustc (what Termux ships) can build them.
#
# This is the subset of the upstream PR the build half compiles. omp itself is
# never rebuilt here, so the coding-agent launcher and clipboard hunks are not
# vendored.
#
# The desktop-adapter pass-through this patch used to carry is gone: v18.7.0
# onward keep the shared native entrypoint importable with a missing
# DesktopSession and defer its rejection to the first desktop use.
#
# Applied by apply_patch in dev/omp-termux-dev (git apply, CHANGELOG hunks excluded).
